# Virtualenvs, byte-caches and build cruft: none of it belongs in the throwaway build repo.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log

# Build-tool working files under the cache dir. The ONE exception is the ~444KB filtered-edge
# cache: it is the only data input the runners need (they never see the 497MB dump), so it is
# force-included below.
tools/conceptnet_build/.cache/*
!tools/conceptnet_build/.cache/edges.tsv.gz
build.lock

# Verdict caches (local ground truth, shard outputs, merged results) are transient build artifacts,
# never committed. The runners regenerate their shards from edges.tsv.gz alone.
verdicts*.tsv

# The raw ConceptNet dump: far too large for git and unneeded on the runners.
*.csv.gz

# Local copies of the authored bank and supervised training exports.
# Keep source code, documentation and small demonstration drafts reviewable.
artifacts/forge/bank-*/

# Training data/weights must never be added to an unchecked/public remote.
training/brainbloom/
training-run/
.test-tmp/
artifacts/forge/colab-*/

# Optional, hash-pinned dictionary download; recreated with dictionary-install.
.brainbloom/wordnet.zip
.brainbloom/*.sqlite3*

# --- Public-push hardening -------------------------------------------------
# Everything below is local, regenerable, or far too large for a public remote.
# The engine does not read any of it: the ConceptNet artifact is a frozen literal
# in src/spie/conceptnet_data.py, and corpora are fetched by the installers. See
# DEPLOY.md. Kept broad on purpose so `git add -A` cannot leak ~240 MB of it.

# Local corpora and session state: WordNet/OEWN downloads, the sqlite draft
# history, the corpora/ cache. All recreated by dictionary-install / oewn-install.
.brainbloom/

# Benchmark bundles, coverage runs, bundled platform wheels (~204 MB). Generated.
artifacts/

# setuptools build output and locally generated draft dumps.
build/
drafts/

# Scratch generation experiments and their one-off JSON outputs at the repo root.
_gen_*.py
generated_*.json

# A workshop export that happens to live under examples/. It is an ARRAY of handoff
# bundles, not a single-puzzle object, so test_presentation.py's examples/*.json glob
# load_puzzle()s it and errors. It is scratch, unreferenced by any tracked code, and must
# not ship. The 20 numbered corpus puzzles (examples/[0-9][0-9]_*.json) are unaffected.
examples/workshop-handoff-bundles.json

